  "body": "A bore-side contour with several rings enters only the first ring by its ramp or helix.\r\nEach later ring at the same level goes through the pass link (`ring_link` in\r\n`contour_link.rs`). The link lifts and plunges straight into solid at the plunge feed. The\r\npath has no note.\r\n\r\nMeasured on main: three square bores, entry ramp at 5 degrees, stepdown 2 mm over 6 mm:\r\n6 axial dives (2 later rings, 3 levels), `notes: []`.\r\n\r\nWorkaround: links `level: keep_down`.\r\n\r\nDone means:\r\n- Every ring takes the entry on its first level, and the level transition below it.\r\n- The pass link still feeds straight where the keep-down proof holds.\r\n- A single ring posts the same descent as before.\r\n\r\nProposed labels (a collaborator sets them): bug, source:agent, P3, effort:high, area:2d\r\n",
